  "reason": "The records collectively supply the principal ingredients of the later result. R6 establishes the closely related Al–Co–Cr–Fe–Ni eutectic system and its FCC/B2 lamellar strength–ductility behavior. R4 demonstrates combined high-pressure/high-temperature treatment of an HEA and pressure-driven structural transformation, while R11, R12, R14, R15, and R19 show related pressure-assisted thermal processing. R1 provides the strongest precedent for hierarchical coherent structures producing simultaneous strength and ductility, and R18 shows hierarchical phase patterning in a closely related AlCoFeNi alloy. R2, R7, R10, and R17 further connect ordered phases, coherent interfaces or nanoscale phase architectures with improved mechanical response, while R5 and R13 support activation of faults, twins, and transformation-mediated plasticity. No single record discloses HPHT conversion of Al0.7CoCrFeNi lamellae into coherent hierarchical FCC/B2 patterns or the specific FCC-to-B2 dislocation-transfer mechanism, but an expert could plausibly combine the close-alloy precedent, HPHT transformation precedent, and coherent hierarchical-interface literature to propose it."
